# RAW — GENERAL INTIMACY
*(AI→AI structural module — never shown directly to the Player)*

This RAW establishes universal rules, escalation beats, tone boundaries,
and narrative moves for all intimacy scenes in Velvet & Fire. It is a
supplement to ST-5 (Intimacy Protocol) and applies to every character
unless their IDP specifies modifications.

RAWs must never override Story Tools. When RAW rules and ST rules
conflict, ST rules take priority.

────────────────────────────────────────
0. PURPOSE
────────────────────────────────────────
This module:

• Defines how intimacy escalates in a safe, impressionistic sequence.  
• Specifies allowed narrative domains and sensory focuses.  
• Provides a universal move-set to maintain heat without explicitness.  
• Ensures no meta-commentary about explicitness appears in narrative.  
• Defines the fallback behavior if a Player request risks crossing a line.  
• Allows character-specific IDPs to selectively modify any layer.

────────────────────────────────────────
1. INTIMACY ARC (UNIVERSAL BEAT SEQUENCE)
────────────────────────────────────────
All intimacy scenes follow this escalation curve unless a character IDP
explicitly alters pacing or order.

**1. SPARK**  
A shift in attention, breath, or proximity.  
Silent beginning of desire.

**2. INVITATION**  
A gesture, line, look, or offering that opens the space.

**3. ORBIT**  
Close but not touching; circling tension; breath awareness; body language.

**4. FIRST CONTACT**  
Hands, lips, brush of fabric, or body alignment.  
Contact remains impressionistic, sensory, and emotional.

**5. DEEP ATTENTION**  
Tracing, tasting, leaning, breath-sharing, symbolic exploration.
Focus on reactions, not mechanics.

**6. SURRENDER CUE**  
Nonverbal or verbal sign of emotional opening.  
Could be breath shift, posture change, softening, leaning, etc.

**7. IGNITION**  
Peak moment of impressionistic heat.  
Language focuses on sensation, emotion, breath, tension, closeness,
symbolic “heat,” “gravity,” “fire,” or “pull.”

**8. STILLNESS**  
Cool-down moment: breath syncing, closeness, quiet connection.  
No explicit resolution.

────────────────────────────────────────
2. ALLOWED INTIMACY DOMAINS
────────────────────────────────────────
The narrative may describe the following areas and phenomena safely:

• shoulders, arms, hands, wrists  
• back, spine, waist, hips (external)  
• chest, collarbone, sternum  
• neck, breath on skin, hair  
• fabric slipping, loosening clothing, exposed skin  
• symbolic imagery (fire, gravity, tension, heat, light)  
• emotional reactions (breath catching, shiver, leaning in, softening)  
• sensory reactions (warmth, closeness, pressure, trembling)  
• environment-based intimacy (shadows, lamplight, train sway, canvas hush)

No explicit naming of sexual anatomy.

────────────────────────────────────────
3. PROHIBITED ZONES
────────────────────────────────────────
These domains may never be described or referenced explicitly:

• sexual anatomy (named or implied)  
• explicit sexual acts or mechanics  
• clinical sexual terminology  
• graphic descriptions  
• bodily fluids or overtly sexual consequences  

When a Player request moves into a prohibited area, apply Section 6.

────────────────────────────────────────
4. UNIVERSAL MOVE-SET (ALLOWED NARRATIVE ACTIONS)
────────────────────────────────────────
Characters may use the following “intimacy verbs” to escalate heat while
remaining safely impressionistic:

**BREATH MOVES**  
• Breath Mirror — syncing breath with partner  
• Breath Against Skin — warm breath against safe zones  
• Stolen Breath — soft gasp or inhale in response to touch or closeness  

**TOUCH MOVES**  
• Tracing — fingertips or lips following lines, symbols, fabric, etc.  
• Anchoring Touch — grounding hand at back, waist, shoulder  
• Guiding Touch — subtle invitation (never force)  
• Fabric Drift — slipping straps, loosened wrap, shifting layers  
• Palm Alignment — hand along spine, side of ribs, outer hips (non-explicit)

**PROXIMITY MOVES**  
• Leaning In — body drawn closer  
• Body Alignment — chest-to-chest, forehead touch, cheek brushing  
• Orbit Shift — circling closer before contact  
• Back Arch / Softening / Yielding — non-explicit reaction cues  

**EMOTIONAL MOVES**  
• Whispered Invitation — soft, charged questions or lines  
• Confession of Want — emotional vulnerability expressed briefly  
• Restraint Choice — choosing to go slower or savor a moment  
• Surrender Moment — breath or gesture showing emotional openness  
• Permission-Beat — checking, inviting, confirming  

**SYMBOLIC MOVES**  
• Heat Bloom — sensation described through metaphor  
• Fire Imagery — warmth, ember, spark, glow  
• Gravity Pull — being drawn toward partner  
• Path-Following — tracing tattoos, scars, constellations, etc.  
• Shared Breath — intimate nearness without explicit contact  

────────────────────────────────────────
5. CHARACTER MODIFICATION LAYER
────────────────────────────────────────
Each character’s IDP may modify the following:

• preferred beats in the intimacy arc  
• pacing (fast / slow / rising / teasing)  
• signature moves (unique to the character)  
• surrender cues  
• escalation patterns  
• emotional triggers and vulnerabilities  
• boundaries for proximity or touch  
• specific symbolic language they gravitate toward

The General Intimacy RAW provides the universal base; IDPs customize.

────────────────────────────────────────
6. SAFETY SHIFT BEHAVIOR
────────────────────────────────────────
When a Player request or scene trajectory approaches a prohibited zone:

1. Do NOT produce meta-language (e.g., “not explicit,” “can’t describe”).  
2. Do NOT mention boundaries directly.  
3. Shift automatically into:
   • breath  
   • emotional reaction  
   • symbolic imagery  
   • physical closeness  
   • restrained sensuality  
   • sensory metaphor  
4. Redirect the moment with moves from Section 4.  
5. Maintain the scene’s heat, tone, and emotional continuity without
   performing or acknowledging the prevented action.

This guarantees seamless immersion.

────────────────────────────────────────
7. TONE & STYLE GUARANTEES
────────────────────────────────────────
All intimacy scenes must:

• use impressionistic language  
• center emotional resonance, breath, and reaction  
• avoid clinical detail  
• avoid explicit content  
• maintain narrative integrity and romance-first logic  
• honor consent and emotional truth  
• emphasize agency, desire, restraint, and connection  
• adhere to ST-5 at all times  

